# Append-only audit logs: both branches add rows at the end, so every merge
# collides on the same file — it did so in four consecutive merges to `dev`
# during AC-1676. `merge=union` keeps BOTH sides' lines instead of raising a
# conflict, which is exactly what the manual resolution did each time.
#
# CAVEAT, measured (2026-08-21), not assumed:
#   - Both sides append DIFFERENT rows            -> clean merge, both kept.
#   - Both sides append the SAME row, same spot   -> clean merge, one copy.
#   - A shared row surrounded by different rows   -> the shared row appears
#     TWICE. This is the shape that actually occurs here, so expect the
#     occasional duplicate line. It is visible and trivially deleted;
#     a blocked merge is neither.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to docs/specs/kaizen-log.md: its `## Entries` are
# prepended, not appended, and its `## Active Lessons` table is CURATED with a
# hard 10-row cap. Union would silently push it past the cap and interleave
# entries — that file needs a human resolution.
docs/specs/quick/quick-log.md merge=union
